cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or these benchmark materials, please cite it as below."
title: "SpeechSplice: Pronunciation Control in Encoder–Decoder LLM-based TTS by Replacing Encoder Hidden States"
abstract: >-
  SpeechSplice controls pronunciation in encoder-decoder LLM-based
  text-to-speech without training and without modifying model weights, by
  replacing entity-position hidden states at the encoder output with
  pronunciation-bearing vectors. This repository contains the implementation, a
  word-replacement pronunciation benchmark in six languages, the listening-test
  materials and item-level results, and pre-computed evaluation outputs for
  each table.
